(7703424, 1264844, 67145, '<td valign="top">i was feeling on first view that you were pushing the definition of panorama in photography . <br/>so i googled it .. <br/><i>"Panoramic photography is a technique of photography, using specialized equipment or software, that captures images with horizontally elongated fields of view. It is sometimes known as wide format photography. The term has also been applied to a photograph that is cropped to a relatively wide aspect ratio, like the familiar letterbox format in wide-screen video."</i> <br/> <br/>this looked more like a 6x4 dimension to me which wouldnt be a panorama at all ... so i measured the sides of your image on computer monitor and came at an approx 12x7 dimension   .. then using the rectangular marquee tool in photoshop put that dimension over an existing 6x4 photo i had up .. <br/>surprisingly it took on a much more panoramic appearance . <br/>how interesting that the eye can be fooled .. and the brain of course ..<br/> <br/>anyway .. i felt i owed you the time i took to see if this indeed did satisfy the challenge .. and it did .. mainly because i really like the photo and wanted to give you a high vote .. <br/>lucky for you .. !! .. ;)<br/>loving the point of view btw .. and that gorgeous blue water ... also whats nice is the sun shining in the distance .. almost like an invitation ..</td>', 'i was feeling on first view that you were pushing the definition of panorama in photography . so i googled it .. "Panoramic photography is a technique of photography, using specialized equipment or software, that captures images with horizontally elongated fields of view. It is sometimes known as wide format photography. The term has also been applied to a photograph that is cropped to a relatively wide aspect ratio, like the familiar letterbox format in wide-screen video."  this looked more like a 6x4 dimension to me which wouldnt be a panorama at all ... so i measured the sides of your image on computer monitor and came at an approx 12x7 dimension   .. then using the rectangular marquee tool in photoshop put that dimension over an existing 6x4 photo i had up .. surprisingly it took on a much more panoramic appearance . how interesting that the eye can be fooled .. and the brain of course .. anyway .. i felt i owed you the time i took to see if this indeed did satisfy the challenge .. and it did .. mainly because i really like the photo and wanted to give you a high vote .. lucky for you .. !! .. ;)loving the point of view btw .. and that gorgeous blue water ... also whats nice is the sun shining in the distance .. almost like an invitation ..', '2021-10-14 23:31:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(7703425, 1264715, 67145, '<td valign="top">WOW and WOW again .. !! .. <br/>that sky is EXCEPTIONAL .. loving the beautiful shapes formed by the clouds as if they are reaching up .. like arms .. almost beseeching ..  <br/>the sky behind the clouds with the yellow glow is sublime .. :)</td>', 'WOW and WOW again .. !! .. that sky is EXCEPTIONAL .. loving the beautiful shapes formed by the clouds as if they are reaching up .. like arms .. almost beseeching ..  the sky behind the clouds with the yellow glow is sublime .. :)', '2021-10-14 23:33:35.000000', NULL, 1),
